From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 05:04:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 126/160] hjviewer: review fixes, ready lane (1.9)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- policy keys: the sleep and hibernate policy is looked up under the bare
  GUID that Group Policy's power.admx writes, and under the braced form;
  policy_keys() builds both and has a test.
- the card draws its rows once the core facts and the password state are
  in; the relay row stays "checking" until hjv-api answers, which now has
  an 8 s limit before it reads as unreachable (D19).
- [절전 안 함] that fails after its first write keeps the stored values,
  so [되돌리기] can undo what was written (D13); a Fake case covers it.
- the fix result is reported once, to the card's next read; a refusal
  without a policy key keeps [절전 안 함] and adds the policy's
  [방법 보기] instead of the T4-44 policy row.
- the header says "Could not check." instead of "All set." when a row of
  taking connections is unread and none is missing.
- the card's dialogs drop quietly when the overlay is not ready, as the
  account file's do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
